			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1492,
				5
			],
			"Message": "chore(Mountain): Update documentation and telemetry configuration for v2.2\n\nSync CHANGELOG.md and README.md to reflect the v2.2 correctness pass, detailing the reduction of Cocoon circuit-breaker rejections to zero via the new `-32004` JSON-RPC error code for benign 404s. Expand documentation on the `sky:replay-events` handler, terminal ring buffers, and the modularization of the IPC layer.\n\nIn `build.rs`, propagate new OTLP telemetry environment variables (`OTLPEndpoint`, `OTLPEnabled`, `Capture`, `Trace`) to the compilation target, enabling granular trace filtering and endpoint configuration. Update `scripts/cocoon/bootstrap-fork.js` to emit structured OTLP spans for bootstrap milestones, aligning the extension host instrumentation with the new backend tracing capabilities. Minor formatting adjustments applied to `capabilities/default.json`.",
			"SHA": "5bca3dde328711d9c6f263697f20d507a847c0cf"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-03T08:20:56Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1492,
				9
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Atomize IPC layer and inject W3C trace context\n\nDecompose monolithic IPC handler files (`AdvancedFeatures`, `DevLog`, `StatusReporter`, `WindAirCommands`, `WindServiceAdapters`) into their dedicated sibling directories, aligning with the project's strict file-per-command modularization strategy. This eliminates single-source files exceeding 30KB and prepares the `Source/IPC` layer for granular testing and independent component evolution.\n\nIntroduce `EmitWithTraceparent` to instrument outbound Tauri events with W3C `traceparent` headers. This bridge stamps `_traceparent` fields onto JSON payloads in debug builds, enabling the `Sky` UI layer to correlate frontend event handlers with backend OTLP spans. Release builds bypass this overhead via `cfg!(debug_assertions)` gating.\n\nUpdate remaining modules (`ConfigurationBridge`, `WindAdvancedSync`) to enforce explicit `::Struct` and `::Fn` qualification patterns, resolving potential symbol shadowing during the transition to the atomized architecture.",
			"SHA": "c96e22222b3ced5e16e63c598d8d953340bd7793"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-03T08:20:42Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1496,
				3
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Modularize SCM and TreeView command surfaces\n\nDecompose the monolithic `SourceControlManagement.rs` and `TreeView.rs` command handlers into discrete modules, aligning with the project's strict file-per-command naming convention. The previous implementation bundled all Tauri command logic into single files with extensive inline documentation, violating the separation of concerns required for the growing IPC layer.\n\nKey modifications:\n- **SourceControlManagement.rs**: Replaced 260-line file with a module manifest exporting 7 stub modules (`GetAllSourceControlManagementState`, `ExecuteSCMCommand`, etc.). Retained high-level architectural docs while moving implementation details to dedicated files.\n- **TreeView.rs**: Replaced 302-line file with a module manifest exporting 8 stub modules (`GetTreeViewChildren`, `RefreshTreeView`, etc.). Preserved references to `TreeViewProvider` trait integration points.\n- **Keybinding.rs**: Refactored documentation comments to strictly adhere to the `Command::Function` naming pattern and fix formatting inconsistencies.\n\nThis structural change enables independent development of specific IPC commands, facilitates granular testing, and prevents symbol shadowing issues as the codebase scales. The modular approach mirrors the recent refactorings in `PublishNotification` and `CommandProvider` modules, ensuring consistency across the Mountain binary initialization path.",
			"SHA": "96e824c731d69abcf06c33c53bb3e17f19b3c8e8"
		}
	],
